1	/**
2	 * Shared reap loop — drains completed executions from the broker,
3	 * routes by handle.kind, and dispatches side-effects.
4	 *
5	 * Called once per orchestrator cycle after the claim and review-fix
6	 * concerns have submitted their work. Any orchestrator can drain any
7	 * completion — dispatch is opportunistic, not pinned to the submitter.
8	 *
9	 * Routing:
10	 *   kind=impl       → dispatchExecutorResult (task YAML mutation)
11	 *   kind=review-fix → emit review_dispatch_complete event
12	 *
13	 * Error handling: individual dispatch errors are emitted as events and
14	 * the item is nacked (returned to the queue). Non-throwing.
15	 */
